From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll, kernelbase: preferred UI languages are kept, merged and used for resources

SetProcessPreferredUILanguages and SetThreadPreferredUILanguages kept
nothing, and every Get*PreferredUILanguages call returned the UI language
alone ("returning a dummy value (current locale)", among the most frequent
fixmes); GetThreadUILanguage and SetThreadUILanguage were stubs. Programs
that pick their UI language (installers, Office, Java and .NET programs
with satellite resources) could not, and the resource loader never saw
their choice.

- The process's and each thread's lists are kept (up to five languages,
  by name or id; NULL clears; an unknown language or more than five is
  ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER); a thread's goes with it.
- GetThreadPreferredUILanguages: MUI_THREAD_LANGUAGES gives the thread's
  list alone (possibly empty); MUI_MERGE_USER_FALLBACK the thread's, the
  process's, the user's (or else the system's) and the system's;
  MUI_MERGE_SYSTEM_FALLBACK adds each language's neutral one; with no
  merge flag, the first list that is set. An empty list is "\0\0", count 0.
- The user's list: Control Panel\Desktop PreferredUILanguages (the MUI
  override), else Control Panel\International\User Profile Languages, else
  the UI language followed by the Linux LANGUAGE preference list
  (de_DE:fr:en), else the UI language.
- Resources: FindResource/LoadString with no language now try the thread's
  and the process's preferred languages (and their neutral ones) before the
  user's and the system's, as the MUI resource loader does.
- GetThreadUILanguage gives the first of the merged list;
  SetThreadUILanguage sets the thread's list to that language.

Wine's kernel32 locale tests: one todo_wine (SetThreadUILanguage) passes
and is removed; resource tests: no change.

Gate: test/uilangs-gate.sh (64- and 32-bit; the lists, the merge flags,
another thread, strings loaded in three languages as the lists change, the
LANGUAGE list). Mutants SG_MUTANT_THREAD_LANGS_IGNORED (ntdll/locale.c),
SG_MUTANT_RESOURCE_LANGS_IGNORED (ntdll/resource.c).
